To further reduce unallocated GPUs, combine three new strategies:  
(1) Explicitly prioritize node "closeout" (using all GPUs on a node) and leave only remnant GPU counts that match dominant job shapes in the workload mix;  
(2) Strongly penalize placements that create "stranded" GPU slots (e.g., leaving a single GPU on an 8-GPU node when no jobs ever require a single GPU), using a dynamic lookup from the actual demand histogram;  
